WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.238 --> 00:00:02.094
- [Narrator] The very
thought of Thanksgiving

00:00:02.094 --> 00:00:04.670
drums up foods worth salivating over,

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.353
like stuffing, mashed
potatoes and of course,

00:00:07.353 --> 00:00:08.353
the Tofurky?

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.520
But this Thanksgiving veggie substitute

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.426
wasn't just whipped up overnight.

00:00:13.426 --> 00:00:16.179
It actually took years of trial and error.

00:00:16.179 --> 00:00:18.212
So we called the guy who invented it.

00:00:18.212 --> 00:00:21.421
(phone ringing)

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:22.953
- [Tibbott] I am Seth Tibbott,

00:00:22.953 --> 00:00:25.837
and I am the inventor of Tofurky.

00:00:25.837 --> 00:00:27.732
- [Narrator] Seth Tibbott
was living in Oregon.

00:00:27.732 --> 00:00:29.854
He was a teacher and a
self-professed hippie

00:00:29.854 --> 00:00:32.771
who lived somewhere,
shall we say, unusual.

00:00:32.771 --> 00:00:35.071
- [Tibbott] I built my
own three-story treehouse

00:00:35.071 --> 00:00:37.017
out of scavenged wood.

00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:39.050
- [Narrator] He was also
a serious vegetarian.

00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:42.850
So serious, that he started
his very own tempeh-making company.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.293
- [Tibbott] And I made soy
tempeh, five grain tempeh

00:00:45.293 --> 00:00:47.869
and a sausage tempeh called temperoni,

00:00:47.869 --> 00:00:51.815
and I just made tempeh
for the first 15 years.

00:00:51.815 --> 00:00:53.424
- [Narrator] But there was a problem.

00:00:53.424 --> 00:00:55.683
- [Tibbott] Which was
finding something to eat

00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:57.464
at my own Thanksgiving.

00:00:57.464 --> 00:00:58.937
- [Narrator] You see, at the time,

00:00:58.937 --> 00:01:01.583
there were no main dishes
for vegetarians available.

00:01:01.583 --> 00:01:04.150
So Seth set out to solve the problem,

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.063
and it wasn't so easy.

00:01:06.063 --> 00:01:08.177
First, he created a stuffed pumpkin.

00:01:08.177 --> 00:01:10.233
- [Tibbott] The stuffed
pumpkin was the famous one

00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.754
that we still talk about.

00:01:11.754 --> 00:01:13.437
The whole thing on the pumpkin was that

00:01:13.437 --> 00:01:15.635
it collapsed in the oven, and it seemed

00:01:15.635 --> 00:01:18.363
more like a side dish than a main dish.

00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:19.579
- [Narrator] Then there was...

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.662
- [Tibbott] The gluten
roast, which was really

00:01:21.662 --> 00:01:24.138
an all day thing, took like eight hours.

00:01:24.138 --> 00:01:27.197
Literally, it was just too tough to cut

00:01:27.197 --> 00:01:29.732
with any kind of implement that we had,

00:01:29.732 --> 00:01:32.423
other than a chainsaw, which
we did not bring to the table.

00:01:32.423 --> 00:01:33.952
- [Narrator] Eventually, Seth teamed up

00:01:33.952 --> 00:01:35.197
with his friend, Hans.

00:01:35.197 --> 00:01:38.771
- [Tibbott] He was
making these tofu roasts.

00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:41.184
Had a little bit of
gravy in there with them.

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:45.357
We added the drumettes because
we were mimicking the turkey

00:01:45.357 --> 00:01:48.955
and marketed it under the name Tofurky.

00:01:48.955 --> 00:01:51.341
- [Narrator] Throughout the
years, the recipe evolved.

00:01:51.341 --> 00:01:54.410
- [Tibbott] We soon realized
that this is a vegan feast,

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.626
and vegan plants don't have legs.

00:01:57.626 --> 00:02:00.207
So yeah, it's been a long journey,

00:02:00.207 --> 00:02:03.170
a long, strange tempeh
trip, as a hippie would say.

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:04.246
- [Narrator] And now—

00:02:04.246 --> 00:02:05.920
- [Tibbott] Around here, we call turkey

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.521
a Tofurky substitute.

00:02:07.521 --> 00:02:10.021
(jazzy music)

